&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open source AI tools for niche software development are growing 41% YoY (Redmonk, 2026). Why? Privacy, compliance, and cost. Companies like MedTechAI now self-host Llama-3 with private data for $280/month—versus $3,600+ for SaaS copilots. The trade-off: setup time and maintenance.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Codeium’s open core is now the fastest-growing option in health tech. 67% of surveyed teams prefer it for HIPAA compliance. But don’t expect plug-and-play magic. Self-hosted AI needs proper MLOps, GPU infrastructure, and routine dataset curation. Still, for teams with strict data needs, it’s the only way to build at speed without regulatory nightmares.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;41%YoY growth in open source AI adoption (Redmonk, 2026)&lt;/p&gt;

