&lt;p&gt;Is self-hosted AI worth it for small teams?Self-hosted AI tools offer superior privacy and compliance but require significant setup. For teams with strict data needs, self-hosting pays off; otherwise, SaaS copilots are easier to deploy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Can AI replace human developers in niche software?No. AI code assistants speed up routine work, but human expertise is essential for business logic, compliance, and integration. Hybrid teams consistently outperform AI-only approaches (McKinsey, 2026).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In 2026, AI tools for niche software development aren’t just a productivity hack. They’re a wedge. The teams that tune, test, and collaborate with AI are lapping those who don’t. You can still build software the 2016 way—if you like burning money. The future is vertical, hybrid, and intensely specific. Ignore this, and your next release will be your last.&lt;/p&gt;




