&lt;p&gt;Accurate attendance tracking is an important part of managing monthly employee payroll. When working days, present days, absences, or unpaid leave change, the estimated salary can change as well.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F4rnk4w6mzwlpa57j62ks.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F4rnk4w6mzwlpa57j62ks.png" alt=" " width="800" height="400"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;salary attendance calculator&lt;/strong&gt; offers a simple way to estimate employee pay using attendance information without repeatedly performing manual calculations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Key Attendance Details
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When estimating monthly salary, you may need to consider:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Total working days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee present days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Absent or unpaid leave days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Applicable salary policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

